      {
        "id": 25602,
        "name": "legend",
        "username": "orumedominic",
        "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/o/3da27b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2026-09-08T09:07:59.674Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Not what it did.<br>\nLogs cover that. What it tried and was stopped from doing.</p>\n<p>I hit this building a spend-limited agent wallet. The refusals turned out to<br>\nmatter more than the payments, and I could not find a good way to hand<br>\nsomeone proof that a refusal actually happened.</p>\n<p>What I ended up with: every attempt, allowed or refused, becomes one<br>\nhash-chained receipt saying what was tried and which rule decided it.</p>\n<p>The limits are assertMsg fences in the Daml, so the refusal is the ledger\u2019s, not<br>\nmy app saying so about itself. You can check a chain here with nothing<br>\ninstalled: <a href=\"https://dominicrume.github.io/cantor8_kya_rails/\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Check a payment record | KYA Rails</a></p>\n<p>But I might be solving something nobody else has.</p>\n<p>Has anyone ever asked you to prove your app didn\u2019t do something?<br>\nWhat did you show them?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "posts_count": 4,
        "updated_at": "2026-09-10T21:40:13.815Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
